[d45a — the symbolic-m closure of kappa: the identification pipeline
  run with the mass as a FORMAL VARIABLE]
  banner: EXACT symbolic arithmetic — every matrix entry is a pair of
  polynomials in m (real, imaginary) with Fraction coefficients; the
  Delta-series is a list of such pairs; ZERO floats (no mpmath import,
  no float literal, no tolerance — every gate is polynomial equality).
  Scope: the committed d44d SINGLETON identification, ORD = 4, L = 12,
  both rules (EXC read at Delta^2, LT at Delta^4), tau over r = 1..4 —
  the tau_D_sg0/kappa_pipeline code path ported structurally; the slab
  arms are m-pointwise-verified at #353 and inherit by the A5 weight-
  independence note (declared NOT re-run symbolically; pin section 4).
  DIVISION AUDIT (the pin's failure mode, verified in the port): the
  only divisions anywhere are by integer constants — the 1/2 hopping
  normalization and the 1/k! factorials, entering as exact Fractions;
  the Neumann inversion starts at the identity (gated constant-free
  below by assertion); the polynomial layer defines NO division of
  polynomials, so an m-dependent division would raise TypeError.
  Exact-zero dropping replaces the committed numeric dust drops (an
  identically-zero entry carries no information; mathematically inert).
  Regression sources (read-only): the KTAB rationals from
  v10/data/d44d_slab_kappa_exact.out (KG2) and the REF_LT signed
  channel table from v10/code/d44d_slab_kappa_exact.py (T5).
  Ring-homomorphism note (YG0): evaluation m -> m0 is a homomorphism
  Q[m] -> Q, so the derived polynomials evaluated at m0 ARE the
  pipeline outputs at mass m0; agreement with the committed grid is
  the regression content.
  Deterministic: no RNG, no wall clock, no environment reads; sorted
  iteration at every print; rerun byte-identical (YG4).

